WHAT I WOULD LIKE

If this ends up in something you make, mention where it came from.

    Spatial Systems Atlas by Grig Bilham
    https://github.com/openspatials/spatial-systems-atlas
    https://openspatials.com/msf/atlas/

Either address is enough. That is a request, not a condition, and nothing happens
if you skip it.

If you quote a figure, give the date you took it. The map is rebuilt as the
research grows and the numbers move.

THE ONE PART THAT IS NOT MINE TO GIVE

The research data contains 8,514 short quotations from other parties'
specifications and documentation, each carrying the address it came from, the
document title and the date it was retrieved. A median quotation is 15 words and
the longest is 68.

They are there so you can check a claim instead of trusting it. They belong to
their sources, and CC0 does not reach them.
